 "title": "Morris's No. 24, Madrid, 30 December 1814: the heading and the first sentence",
 "caption": "The coded heading and lines 1 to 4 of No. 24 (NARA RG 59, M31 roll 14, frame 0220), decoded group by group with the key values alone. Words come out as the code builds them (pre-par-ing, re-com-end-ing, dec-lar-ation); marks under the groups, which double or withdraw letters, are not applied here. Four groups are marked as uncertain: the opening 593.813 (perhaps Sir), 145 (June in the key, where relative is wanted) and 1569 (December in the key, where the United States is wanted). The sign 370 after the full stop has no value.",
 "unit": "code groups",
 "key_note": "Values from Andrew Beling's transcription of a surviving sheet of the State Department code (NARA M97 roll 13, Weber's WE028), with Morris's sixteen blocks of 100 taken in reverse order.",
